dialogue.Feran_Crieur.npc = Clearbreath
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.role = Voice of the oasis
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.accueil = May the wind be gentle to you, traveller. The oasis's needs are written on the board behind me.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.voir = Show me the oasis's needs.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.quoi = How can I help?
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.explication = Each morning, three needs. Take one, fulfil it before the next dawn, and the oasis grows. Water and goods go in the chest on the square, or are handed in here.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.encours = Has the wind carried what you were looking for?
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.rendre = Here is what I bring.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.rendu = The oasis will remember, as sand remembers water.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.aurevoir = May water follow you.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.honni = The wind carried your name here, and it was not gentle. Prove us wrong.
dialogue.Feran_Crieur.racheter = I want to make amends.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.npc = Finedune
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.role = merchant
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.honni = You have muddied the oasis's water. I will not trade with you.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.etranger = The Feran do not trade with strangers. Help the oasis, and we will talk.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.commentAider = How do I make myself known?
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.conseil = The crier by the board always has a need for a stranger. Fulfil one or two, and you will be tolerated.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.voirDemandes = Show me the needs
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.accueil = The tolerated traveller! Waterskins, linen, wind statuettes: all paid in wind feathers.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.ami = For a friend of the oasis, I have living water and feathers from the heights.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.hote = Our host! The elders let me open the reserve: Windwalker linen would suit you.
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.troc = Let's see your wares
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.avance = And for friends?
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.reserve = Open the reserve for me
dialogue.Feran_Marchand.aurevoir = May the wind carry you
dialogue.Feran_Builder.npc = Sanddigger
dialogue.Feran_Builder.role = Builder
dialogue.Feran_Builder.accueil = The sand moves, the hut stays. That is my whole art.
dialogue.Feran_Builder.metier = I raise the huts and mend them after the storms. The sandstone in the deposit becomes our walls.
dialogue.Feran_Builder.chantier = A building site is open: I build while the wind sleeps.
dialogue.Feran_Builder.statut = Here is how the site is going.
dialogue.Feran_Watcher.npc = Duneeye
dialogue.Feran_Watcher.role = Watcher
dialogue.Feran_Watcher.accueil = I watch the sand. The sand lies, but not its shadows.
dialogue.Feran_Watcher.metier = From the wall, I watch the hive. When the sand trembles, the Scaraks are coming.
dialogue.Feran_Watcher.auxArmes = The sand trembles! The Scaraks are upon us, to arms!
dialogue.Feran_Watcher.rumeur = The hive has grown this moon. If no one cuts it back, it will come to drink our water.
dialogue.Feran_WellKeeper.npc = Patientwater
dialogue.Feran_WellKeeper.role = Water carrier
dialogue.Feran_WellKeeper.accueil = Every drop counts, traveller. Every drop.
dialogue.Feran_WellKeeper.metier = I carry water from the spring to the huts. Without water, no Feran. Drink in the shade, never in the sun.
dialogue.Feran_Breeder.npc = Softfeather
dialogue.Feran_Breeder.role = Herder
dialogue.Feran_Breeder.accueil = Gently near the pen: my hens lay better in the calm.
dialogue.Feran_Breeder.metier = I raise the oasis beasts. Eggs, leather, wool: nothing goes to waste in the desert.
dialogue.Feran_Guard.npc = Longfang
dialogue.Feran_Guard.role = Guard
dialogue.Feran_Guard.accueil = Halt. The oasis tolerates you; I watch you.
dialogue.Feran_Guard.metier = I hold the oasis gate. My spear has tasted chitin more often than bread.
dialogue.Feran_Guard.auxArmes = The hive attacks! Hold the gate with me!
dialogue.Feran_Guard.rumeur = Scarak scouts circle the dunes. They are counting our spears.
dialogue.Feran_Elder.npc = Oldwind
dialogue.Feran_Elder.role = Elder
dialogue.Feran_Elder.accueil = Sit down. The wind tells things better to those who sit.
dialogue.Feran_Elder.metier = I remember the lost oases. I tell of them, so that this one will not be lost.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.npc = Highbreeze
dialogue.Feran_Chef.role = Oasis chieftain
dialogue.Feran_Chef.aurevoir = May the wind keep you.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.nouvelles = And the hive?
dialogue.Feran_Chef.nouvellesTexte = It grows when forgotten. Cut it back, and it gets angry. There is no good choice, only courage.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.accepter = I'll take care of it.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.accepte = Go. The wind will wait for you.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.auxArmes = The Scaraks are in the oasis! Defend the water, traveller!
dialogue.Feran_Chef.honni = You have muddied the water. Leave.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etranger = The hive is advancing on the oasis, stranger. It is not to you that I will entrust our water.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.commentAider = How do I earn your trust?
dialogue.Feran_Chef.conseil = The board's needs. When you are tolerated, come back to me.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.voirDemandes = See the needs
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape1 = The basin is emptying: the hive drinks our springs. Bring us eight water essences, and we'll see if the wind likes you.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.donner = Here are eight water essences.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.failDonner = you must be Tolerated by the Feran and carry 8 Water Essences
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape2 = The basin fills. To keep the hive at bay, we need wind: set four wind statues at the spot I'll show you, once you are our friend.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape2EnCours = Four wind statues, no fewer. The merchant sells them if you have none.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape3 = The wind blows. Now strike: a hive entrance has opened nearby. Destroy its guardians.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape3EnCours = The hive entrance is guarded. Slay them all.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape4 = The hive is angry. Our Windwalker went to see the ziggurat and has not returned. When you are our host, bring them back.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape4EnCours = The Windwalker waits near the ziggurat. Bring them back to the heart of the oasis.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape5 = The Windwalker saw her: the Broodmother has come out of the hive, to the surface. Only a champion of the Feran can slay her.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.etape5EnCours = The Broodmother nests on the surface. Slay her.
dialogue.Feran_Chef.recompense = The Broodmother has fallen. The wind owes you a debt: this bracelet carries a little of it. And the Windwalker saw smoke to the north, in the cold…
dialogue.Feran_Chef.recevoir = Receive the Wind Bracelet
dialogue.Feran_Chef.fin = The wind carries you, champion. To the north, in the snow, some Outlanders have renounced the cult. They will need you.
chain.Feran.step1 = fill the basin (8 Water Essences, Tolerated)
chain.Feran.step2 = place 4 wind statues (Friend)
chain.Feran.step3 = destroy a hive entrance (Friend)
chain.Feran.step4 = escort the Windwalker (Host)
chain.Feran.step5 = slay the Broodmother, then receive the Wind Bracelet (Champion)
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.npc = Chainbreaker
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.role = Voice of the hamlet
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.accueil = Come closer, and speak softly. The cult has ears everywhere. What we need is carved on the board.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.voir = Show me what you need.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.quoi = How can I help you?
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.explication = Three needs each morning. Take one, fulfil it before dawn, and the hamlet holds one more day. The chest on the square takes what you bring back.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.encours = Do you have it? Show me, quickly.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.rendre = Here.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.rendu = Good. No one will know where it came from.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.aurevoir = Don't look back as you leave.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.honni = You smell of the cult. Leave before the others see you.
dialogue.Renonce_Crieur.racheter = I am not one of them. Let me prove it.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.npc = Old Silence
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.role = merchant
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.honni = Not you. Not here.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.etranger = I sell nothing to strangers. Strangers talk to the cult.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.commentAider = How do I earn your trust?
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.conseil = The crier, by the board. Help the hamlet, once, twice. Then we'll see.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.voirDemandes = Show me the needs
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.accueil = Meat, wool, a brazier if you're cold. Everything is paid in frost tears.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.ami = For a friend: mittens, and something to keep the fire going.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.hote = You held the fort. Take what is left of the fugitives' weapons.
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.troc = Let's see your wares
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.avance = And for friends?
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.reserve = Open the reserve for me
dialogue.Renonce_Marchand.aurevoir = Be careful
dialogue.Renonce_Builder.npc = Crackedhand
dialogue.Renonce_Builder.role = Builder
dialogue.Renonce_Builder.accueil = Hush. I nail softly: sound carries far in the snow.
dialogue.Renonce_Builder.metier = I build what the cult burned. Fir, stone, and no totem.
dialogue.Renonce_Builder.chantier = A site is open. I work fast, before the next blizzard.
dialogue.Renonce_Builder.statut = Here's where we are.
dialogue.Renonce_Watcher.npc = Whitewatch
dialogue.Renonce_Watcher.role = Watcher
dialogue.Renonce_Watcher.accueil = Don't stay in the open. They see far, on the snow.
dialogue.Renonce_Watcher.metier = I watch for the cult's fires from the tower. When they all light up, they come for us.
dialogue.Renonce_Watcher.auxArmes = The Marauders! They're here, to arms!
dialogue.Renonce_Watcher.rumeur = The Priest has planted new totems to the north. He wants us back, willing or not.
dialogue.Renonce_Hunter.npc = Softstep
dialogue.Renonce_Hunter.role = Hunter
dialogue.Renonce_Hunter.accueil = You walk too loud. The game hears you, and so does the cult.
dialogue.Renonce_Hunter.metier = I hunt for the hamlet. Without meat, the cold wins. Never stray far from a fire.
dialogue.Renonce_Breeder.npc = Greywool
dialogue.Renonce_Breeder.role = Shepherd
dialogue.Renonce_Breeder.accueil = Close the gate behind you. The mouflons know the way north.
dialogue.Renonce_Breeder.metier = I keep the hamlet's flock. Their wool keeps us warm, their milk keeps us standing.
dialogue.Renonce_Guard.npc = Broadback
dialogue.Renonce_Guard.role = Guard
dialogue.Renonce_Guard.accueil = Are you with us, or with them? Answer fast.
dialogue.Renonce_Guard.metier = I hold the fort tower. I wore their colours, once. Never again.
dialogue.Renonce_Guard.auxArmes = The cult comes to take its own back! No one leaves with them!
dialogue.Renonce_Guard.rumeur = The Marauders are sharpening their blades. They don't like those who renounce.
dialogue.Renonce_Elder.npc = Mother Frost
dialogue.Renonce_Elder.role = Elder
dialogue.Renonce_Elder.accueil = Come close to the fire, child. The cold lies: it says it doesn't hurt.
dialogue.Renonce_Elder.metier = I remember before the cult. I tell the young about it, in a low voice.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.npc = He-Who-Broke
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.role = Forsworn sorcerer
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.aurevoir = Stay close to the fires.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.nouvelles = And the cult?
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.nouvellesTexte = It does not forgive. But it fears fire, and people who no longer fear it.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.accepter = I'll take care of it.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.accepte = Go. And speak of us to no one.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.auxArmes = They're coming to take us back! Defend the hamlet!
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.honni = You smell of their totems. Leave.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etranger = A stranger… The cult often sends strangers. Prove you are not one of them.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.commentAider = How do I earn your trust?
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.conseil = The board. Help the hamlet. Then we'll talk.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.voirDemandes = See the needs
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape1 = Fugitives arrive every night, starving. Bring eight cooked meats, and they'll see one can live without the cult.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.donner = Here are eight cooked meats.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.failDonner = you must be Tolerated by the Forsworn and carry 8 Cooked Meat
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape2 = They eat, thank you. But the Priest plants his totems around us, and the fugitives hear him at night. When you are our friend, slay him.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape2EnCours = The Priest guards his altar. Slay him.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape3 = The Priest has fallen, his totems are silent. To flee further, we need boats: thirty-two fir trunks in the deposit.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape3EnCours = Thirty-two fir trunks, in the deposit. The boats are waiting.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape4 = The boats are ready, and the Marauders have seen it. They will come one night. When you are our host, hold the fort with us.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape4EnCours = Tonight, the Marauders will come. Stay at the fort, with our guards.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.etape4Attente = The boats are ready, and the Marauders have seen it. But we have no fort to hold yet: help the hamlet grow until the tower rises.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.recompense = You held the fort. I wove this mantle with what was left of my magic: the cold will bite you no more. I give it only to a champion.
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.recevoir = Receive the Frost Mantle
dialogue.Renonce_Chef.fin = The cold lets you pass now. Further on, beyond the passes, there is a monastery. What the Void keeps there, I do not want to know.
chain.Renonce.step1 = feed the fugitives (8 Cooked Meat, Tolerated)
chain.Renonce.step2 = slay the Priest and his totems (Friend)
chain.Renonce.step3 = bring back the boats (32 Fir Trunks, Friend)
chain.Renonce.step4 = hold the fort against the Marauders (Host)
chain.Renonce.step5 = receive the Frost Mantle (Champion)
